      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The critical difference in perspective is that \"necessary stabilization\" in the context of government support is often championed to directly support specific demand side needs currently being out of reach for the general public. Supporters argue this targeted support can keep crucial parts of the economy stable *while* the underlying supply issues are being fixed.\n\nHowever, you are correct that a rigid adherence to pure supply and demand, favoring strict fiscal discipline like in the conservative view, often predicts that aggressive government support will definitely lead to the very inflationary outcome you are concerned about.",
